+<section id="02-in-place-editing" aria-labelledby="heading-02-in-place-editing">
+<h2 id="heading-02-in-place-editing">Edit content in place — updated October 8</h2>
+<p><strong>Intentional entry, one section:</strong> choose <strong>Edit section</strong> or Edit section here. Type, replace, paste and format directly in rendered headings, paragraphs, lists, tables and literal code within the existing document scroll surface. A named section boundary identifies the editing scope; surrounding content remains readable and read-only.</p>
+<p>Formatting appears contextually on selection or a block-action request. Keyboard and contextual routes retain the selection and restore the caret when dismissed. <strong>No raw Markdown pane, separate preview, source/preview toggle or split editor.</strong> Literal code is document content; conflict inspection is a separate read-only recovery task.</p>
+<ul>
+<li><strong>Save and Save As:</strong> explicit Save returns to reading only after acknowledgment. Save As retains its existing Save a copy semantics and leaves the original dirty. Cancellation or failure preserves the draft. Unsaved and recovery acknowledgments remain distinct.</li>
+<li><strong>Dirty exits and conflicts:</strong> retain Save / Keep draft / Discard / Cancel guards and revision-aware recovery. Disk conflict blocks original Save and keeps Inspect versions / Keep my edit / Save a copy / confirmed Use disk version. See <a href="#15-save-recovery-states">state board 15</a>.</li>
+<li><strong>Undo/Redo and recovery:</strong> preserve source-backed draft transactions, selection and existing schema1 history/recovery. No cross-save Undo promise is added.</li>
+<li><strong>Opaque constructs:</strong> preserve Mermaid, YAML, raw HTML and unknown constructs with their original bytes and safe presentation. Refuse unsafe splits, conversions, deletion or movement with a construct-specific explanation; preserve draft and selection. No source-editor fallback.</li>
+</ul>
+<p class="scope"><strong>CRLF Save remains DEFERRED.</strong> The <a href="../../../docs/macos-crlf-save-deferral-20261008.md">recorded user deferral</a> is unchanged; non-LF authoring remains guarded. No fix, successful CRLF acceptance or reopened gate is inferred.</p>
+<p><strong>Evidence and limits:</strong> the <a href="../../../frontend-implementation/evidence/in-place-finish-20261008/report.md">implementation finish report</a> records delivered editing and separate focused/native checks, with unresolved broader regression failures. Final packaged journeys, physical IME, VoiceOver and the full theme/locale/size matrix remain NOT TESTED end-to-end. Platform/visual acceptance is incomplete and user acceptance pending. This static gallery is a design handoff, not native or visual acceptance.</p>
+<p><a href="interaction-spec.md#direct-in-place-editing">Detailed interaction specification</a> · <a href="frontend-handoff.md">Updated frontend handoff</a> · <a href="revision-record.json">Scoped revision and hashes</a>. Option D remains the controlling navigation reference; inherited header arrows in this mixed mockup are superseded.</p>
